  "interpretation": "Original generic placement17DF4/17E68 copies one type-indexed BYTE default from17D0C into record1C. Primary801A uses zero to suppress ordinary type dispatch. In pairwise contact, signed-negative1C bypasses ordinary damage/retirement paths, positive1C is decremented atB706/B72E or mirroredB828/B852, and surviving hits set flagsBIT2 while exhaustion reaches original scoring/retirement. Type103 original string Icarus Gas Laser Bolt reaches one-decrement path; type84 Energy Cube Launcher reaches the two-stage path, with an asymmetric outer Homing Missile12/nonzero22 shortcut that clears durability. Preserve both decrements, zero/negative comparisons and BYTE wrap rather than inventing saturation or one count per collision. Generic direct contact may retire a nonnegative object without decrementing, and neutron/projector/explicit retirement can bypass this protection: negative is not a universal invulnerability proof. Celestial1880A/radial188DA set bit7 on the same signed byte; construction/damage/actor split and clearing readers therefore support a shared durability_or_negative member at Core1C, not a universal set of independent flags. Model default table is only the existing104 BYTE prefix17D0C..17D74; high-type/default adjacent aliases and following6bytes remain unchanged and conditional. Model callbacks use strength thresholds for split/behavior transitions, not a universal timer. No new type seeds, pointer/index/lifetime proof, emulator run or rewritten behavior.",
  "field": {
    "owner": "SG2ObjectCore",
    "name": "durability_or_negative",
    "offset": 28,
    "size": 1,
    "type": "BYTE",
    "meaning": "Signed durability used by ordinary contact damage and primary dispatch. Negative values bypass those ordinary contact paths; zero suppresses primary type dispatch. This is not a universal invulnerability flag or exact one-hit counter."
  },
